```
But note `page` increment only after swipe; resetting page might affect loop max. Fine. But if list didn't actually move (gone due to stale dump weird), we'd restart bottom and may loop? pending unchanged maybe eventually stuck because pending not found then walkUp stops? Let's keep.

Potential infinite loop: After done bump, pending delete, restart bottom; fine. After gone, pending remains; restart bottom; walk from bottom. Could repeatedly return gone if item not actually in list? bumpOne returns "gone" only attempt0 no node; but we call bumpOne only when visible in parsed nodes, so node should exist on current screen unless list moved. After restart bottom, if item truly not present, for loop won't call; eventually walk ends and pending remains; walkUp compares pending size unchanged → break. Fine.

But restarting inside a pass after a bump: before size may change, okay.

scrollToEdge threshold change stuck>=1. Also stop messages? We'll modify.

